title: Executive Action
subtitle: What the President can do alone.
tags: govt_action
new-page: true
view-if: executive_timer <= 0 and white_house == "D"
choose-if: capital >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: We need at least 2 capital.
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; capital -= 2; executive_timer = 2

= Executive Action

When Congress will not act, the executive branch can do a little. Courts and successors can undo it.

- @regulation: Agency rulemaking.
- @appoint: Judicial and agency appointments.
- @immig: Immigration and enforcement priorities.
- @norms: Restore institutional norms.

@regulation
subtitle: Real, but reversible.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 3; pop_mod += 0.1; mod_dissent += 1; prog_dissent -= 2

Rules take effect. Lawsuits follow.

@appoint
subtitle: Long-lasting.
on-arrival: stability += 3; enthusiasm += 2; maga += 1

Courts matter, and so do the people who staff the government.

@immig
subtitle: A flashpoint.
on-arrival: enthusiasm += 3; prog_dissent -= 3; mod_dissent += 3; far_right += 2; maga += 2

The politics are as hard as the law.

@norms
subtitle: Strengthens institutions.
on-arrival: stability += 5; media_trust += 3; enthusiasm -= 1

Not a vote-winner. But it matters.
